  "chapter": 745,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 91 Chapter 745\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 4241-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to\n        authorizing retail licenses to purchase  beer,  wine  or  liquor\n        with a business payment card\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  The  sale  of alcoholic beverages is a highly regulated industry. Some\nof the regulations stem from prohibition era rules. Some, while they may\nseem innocuous, are important  to  ensuring  that  there  is  a  robust,\ncompetitive  marketplace  in  New  York  State.  Even  today, while some\nrestrictions remain necessary, the industry needs to be able  to  evolve\nwith  the  changing technological atmosphere. One such aspect is the use\nof a credit card to pay for product rather than requiring cash.\n \n  In today's society, the vast majority of consumers use  some  form  of\nelectronic  fund  transfers  rather  than  cash.  There is no reason why\nretail licensees should not also be allowed  to  use  these  alternative\nmethods  of  payment.  However,  with the use of these methods comes the\nimposition of fees, which can pose concerns. We need to ensure that  all\nsimilarly situated parties are subject to the same terms and conditions.\nAllowing  larger  wholesalers  to  absorb a surcharge would give them an\neconomic advantage over smaller  wholesalers  who  would  struggle  with\nthose  costs.  Such  an  unequal  playing  field would have a pernicious\neffect on the competitive marketplace.\n \n  The bill presented to me attempts to allow wholesalers  and  distribu-\ntors  of  beer, wine, and liquor to accept payment from retail licensees\nthrough the use of a business payment card. There are certain  technical\nissues  specific  to  the  alcoholic  beverage  industry  that  were not\naddressed, and additionally, due to concerns raised that are  unique  to\nliquor  and  wine,  those wholesalers and retailers will be removed from\nthe bill's provisions. I have reached an agreement with the  Legislature\nto address those issues and alleviate the concerns. Based on that infor-\nmation, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2019
 },
